events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Decision record for #5891 — Decomposition Item 1 of #5685 (DoS suite & performance benchmark programme), scoped by triage task 10293 (2026-11-08) and produced by queue task 13155.\n\nSettles, for the shared load & workload generator:\n\n- **Generator core**: one core in `pkgs/id/tests/common/loadgen.rs` (the existing shared test-support home; benches reach the same source via `#[path]`), seeded/deterministic, closed-loop vs open-loop pacing, op-count phase boundaries.\n- **Target abstraction**: one trait, three surfaces — `InProcess` (the `world_bench` pattern), `LocalSocket` (what the #5894 baseline measures), `Iroh` (loopback by default; remote only behind an explicit operator flag).\n- **Profiles**: workloads are data (the five honest operation families); honest profiles are the #5894 scales; adversarial behaviours (`churn`, `slowloris`, `amplify`, `bomb`, `garbage`, `exhaust`) are named modifiers on an honest profile, not separate workloads. The scenario catalogue itself stays #5892.\n- **Contracts**: one run header + summary format for benchmark and DoS runs (building on the `world_bench`/`BASELINES.md` key=value convention), and a fixed assertion vocabulary for DoS scenarios (`healthy_within`, `no_wedge`, `honest_throughput_at_least`, `state_bounded`).\n- **Rejected alternatives** (external load tools, per-suite harnesses, a new crate in v1, Criterion) and the invariants sibling tickets consume, plus a 5-step implementation order for follow-on packets.\n\nDocs only; no code changes. Sibling record: #5894 in PR #7620.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796729296&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7662&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7662&signat